## 🌐 Deploying to GitHub Pages

Because this is a 100% client-side application (HTML/CSS/JS + static binary files), it can be hosted **100% free on GitHub Pages** with zero backend infrastructure required.

### Step 1: Initialize Git Repository
```bash
git init
git add .
git commit -m "Initial commit of FrogID v7 Interactive Map Visualization"
```

### Step 2: Push to GitHub
1. Create a new public repository on [GitHub](https://github.com/new) (e.g. `frogid-v7-map`).
2. Link your local repo and push:
```bash
git remote add origin https://github.com/YOUR-USERNAME/frogid-v7-map.git
git branch -M main
git push -u origin main
```

### Step 3: Enable GitHub Pages
1. Go to your repository **Settings** on GitHub.
2. Scroll to the **Pages** section on the left sidebar.
3. Under **Build and deployment** $\rightarrow$ **Source**, select `Deploy from a branch`.
4. Under **Branch**, select `main` / `/ (root)` and click **Save**.
5. Within 1–2 minutes, your live website will be published at:
   `https://YOUR-USERNAME.github.io/frogid-v7-map/`
